{title: 171 - Thine Is the Glory}
{artist: Seventh-day Adventist Hymnal}
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: Eb}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{tag: Jesus Christ}
{tag: }

Verse 1:
[Eb]Thine is [Fm]the [Eb]glory, [Bb]Risen, [Eb]conquering Son;
[Bb]Endless [Eb]is the victory Thou o'er death hast won.
[Eb/G]Angels in bright [Fm]rai [Gm]ment Rolled [Bb]the [Bb7]stone away,
[Eb]Kept the folded grave-clothes [Cm]Where [Ddim]Thy [Eb]bodylay.

Refrain:
[Gm]Thine is [Cm]the glory, Risen, conquering [Eb/Bb]Son;
[F7/A]Endless is [Gm]the victory [Eb]thou [Fm]o'er death hast [Bb]won.

Verse 2:
[Eb]Lo! Jesus meets us. [Bb]Risen [Eb]from the [Bb7/D]tomb,
[Bb]Lovingly [Eb]He greets us, Scatters fear and gloom;
[Eb/G]Let His Church [Fm]with gladness [Bb]hymns of [Bb7]triumph [Eb]sing,
[Eb]For her Lord now liveth; [Bb7]Death [Cm]has [Ddim]lost [Eb]its [Fm]sting.

Verse 3:
[Eb]No more [Fm]we [Eb]doubt Thee, [Bb]Glorious [Eb]Prince of [Bb7/D]life!
[Bb]Life is [Eb]nought without Thee; Aid us in our strife;
[Eb/G]Make us more than [Fm]conquerors [Bb]through Thy [Bb7]deathless [Eb]love
[Eb]Bring us safe through Jordan [Bb7]to [Cm]Thy [Ddim]home [Eb]above.
